From d79fc988201cda9d016a3656b0d2b8e53de2c75b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mms-it-ch <info@mms-it.ch>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 13:35:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 04/12] rtl: add the z/OS port (s390x, LLVM code generator
 only)

rtl/zos: libc based like AIX; all operating system services come from the
C runtime of the Language Environment (ASCII mode, POSIX(ON)).
- types, structure layouts and constants were determined on z/OS with a
  C probe (zos-pascal-llvm: pf1/probe/zosprobe.c); they differ a lot from
  other Unix systems (e.g. O_RDONLY=2, F_OK=8, S_IFMT=$FF000000, struct
  stat with eye catcher, tv_usec after 4 padding bytes)
- errno.inc is generated from errno.h (scripts/gen-errno.py), errno is
  accessed through __errno()
- the heap uses malloc/free (mmap cannot map anonymous memory on z/OS)
- sigset_t is manipulated through the C library
- the Itanium unwind interface and the atomic operations come from a small
  C runtime of the port (zos-pascal-llvm: runtime/*.c, linked with $L)

rtl/s390x: no assembler routines; get_caller_addr etc. produce a fake
backtrace like on wasm32, setjmp/longjmp are not used (LLVM exceptions).

rtl/inc/psabieh.inc: FPC_DummyPotentialRaise in Pascal for s390x.

Assisted-by: Claude Code (Anthropic)
